Package: litirt
Title: IRT-Based Proficiency Level Classification for Literacy and Large-Scale Assessments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last",
           email = "corresponding@email.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements Item Response Theory (IRT)-based proficiency level 
    classification for large-scale literacy and educational assessments. 
    Given IRT theta estimates and user-defined cut scores, litirt classifies 
    respondents into proficiency levels, computes classification accuracy 
    and standard errors of classification, estimates misclassification 
    probabilities, and produces Wright map visualizations with benchmark 
    overlays. The package supports any number of proficiency levels and 
    any IRT model supported by the mirt package. Built-in datasets include 
    simulated data representative of PISA reading literacy and Indonesian 
    AKM (Asesmen Kompetensi Minimum) literacy assessments, enabling 
    immediate demonstration without user-supplied data. Functions are 
    applicable to any assessment context using IRT-based proficiency 
    classification, including educational, psychological, clinical, and 
    organizational measurement.
